SUMMARY:Intro to Canoe Camping
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/intro-canoe-camping)**\n\n
 ***If you've been curious about backcountry canoe camping but unsure where
  to start\, this is a solid entry point.***\n\nWe’ll be heading into the
  iconic Algonquin Park for an easy canoe camping adventure on Joe Lake. It
 ’s a short paddle in\, about 7km total\, with just one 240m portage alon
 g the way. The route offers a good intro to how we carry gear between lake
 s at a steady\, safe and manageable pace.\n\nWe'll launch from Canoe Lake 
 and follow a calm route past narrow channels and rocky shorelines typical 
 of the Canadian Shield. Weather conditions can change quickly\, so we’ll
  pack accordingly and help you plan ahead. Wildlife sightings are common i
 n this area\, so keep your eyes peeled for turtles\, beavers\, and the occ
 asional moose if we’re lucky.\n\nOnce we reach camp\, you can settle in 
 and do what feels right. Swim\, read\, hang out with the group\, or practi
 ce campsite basics like setting up a tarp or hanging food safely.\n\nThis 
 is a chance to experience the magic of the backcountry - falling asleep to
  the sounds of loons\, your tent illuminated by the milky way and learning
  what you need to know without being thrown in the deep end.\n\nWhat's inc
 luded\n\n* Professional\, certified guides\n* Canoes along with all safety
  equipment\n* ‍All camp meals\, cooking equipment and mess kits\n* ‍Te
 nts\n\nSleeping bags and sleeping pads can be rented from WU for a small f
 ee.\n\n**Highlights**\n**Pristine Backcountry -** Escape the crowded city 
 and enter into the serenity of the backcountry.\n**Learn to Portage -** An
  essential skill for conquering the Ontario backcountry\, learn how to por
 tage with confidence from our expert guides.\n**Possible Wildlife Spotting
 ** \\- Bears\\\, moose\\\, beavers\\\, eagles and loons are just some of t
 he creatures that call this area home\\. You'll have a chance to spot some
  from a safe distance for a magical encounter\\.\n\n**Event cost: $349+HST
  - optional transport available.**\n**Register [here.](https://www.wildern
 essunion.com/adventures/intro-canoe-camping)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union
 **\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community th
 at connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you f
 ind your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix
  of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\n
 Attendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - w
 e typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that 
 there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n
 \n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wilde
 rnessunion.com/)***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/314400991/
